  "count": 3,
  "rationale": "Blocking appServer:lateralMovement, memoryDump:credentialAccess and sshKey:credentialAccess makes the target unreachable. Blocking appServer cuts codeRepo, localAdmin, and the appServer route into shareMount. Blocking memoryDump cuts dbLogin, which removes fileServer, secretsManager and serviceAccount, and also cuts one route to monitoringHost. Blocking sshKey stops both rdpLogin and ssoLogin, which removes domainAdmin, hypervisor and the remaining routes to monitoringHost. As a result dbReplica, vaultRead, shareMount and codeRepo are all unreachable. Two blocks are not enough. tokenCache comes straight from entry footholds, so the tokenCache->appServer->codeRepo chain forces blocking tokenCache, appServer or codeRepo. If you block tokenCache, appServer is still reachable through sshKey or memoryDump and feeds both codeRepo and shareMount. If you block appServer or codeRepo, shareMount is still reachable through memoryDump->monitoringHost, and dbReplica through ssoLogin+rdpLogin->domainAdmin. No single extra block closes both remaining routes, so the minimum is 3."
 },
